def three_way_partition(xs, pivot):
    low, mid, high = 0, 0, len(xs) - 1
    while mid <= high:
        if xs[mid] < pivot:
            xs[low], xs[mid] = xs[mid], xs[low]
            low += 1
            mid += 1
        elif xs[mid] > pivot:
            xs[mid], xs[high] = xs[high], xs[mid]
            high -= 1
        else:
            mid += 1
    return low, mid
```

This is the Dutch national flag scheme with three pointers: everything before low is smaller than the pivot, everything from low up to mid equals it, and everything after high is larger. A smaller element is swapped down to position low, and a larger one is swapped up to position high without advancing mid, because the element that arrives at mid has not been examined yet. An equal element is simply stepped over, and when mid passes high the returned pair marks the two group boundaries.

